 "notes": "Lower boundary of the red 'White Dwarfs' exclusion region in Fig. 1 (epsilon-model), traced from the rasterized figure MoneyPlotv2RasterizedMod2New.pdf in the e-print (dark-red boundary line, pixel-calibrated against axis ticks; M_P reference line reproduced at log10(GeV/f)=-19.10 vs expected -19.09). Axes are log10(m_phi/eV) vs log10(GeV/f) with f the standard axion decay constant of L=(g_s^2/32pi^2)(phi/f)GG~, so 1/f is reported directly. Flat part at 1/f~7e-17 GeV^-1 (f~1.4e16 GeV; text quotes f<1.1e16 GeV at 95% CL in the gradient-dominated regime); slope-1 diagonal edge corresponds to epsilon~1.8e-7, matching the quoted 95% CL bound epsilon<2e-7. Diagonal extended analytically (slope fixed by trace) from m~1e-2 eV, where the line is obscured by the SN1987A overlay, to the top of the plotted range (log10(GeV/f)=-4.03 at m~0.5 eV); extension verified against the visible region edge inside the SN band. The upper boundary of the WD band (f>5.5e9 GeV) is not reported; only the lower envelope (headline curve). Orange dashed Chandrasekhar-observation projection excluded. Bound is observational (WD mass-radius data), 2sigma=95% CL, independent of axion dark-matter density.",
